From b7e404836df99329cc4a586671ff4ce94c0c4744 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 11:54:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Quest success rebalance + burst reward taper

- previewSuccess now splits automatic (uncurved) level-derived stats
  from active investment (gear, consumables, facilities, renown, spent
  stat points, elemental, preferred-tag), routing only the latter
  through a new smooth diminishing-returns curve (curveInvestment).
  Replaces an earlier hard-ceiling draft, which was caught during
  design as killing the incentive to keep optimizing once capped.
- Out-levelling a quest still reaches true 95% through the uncurved
  automatic-growth + per-level-gap terms, unchanged.
- New tunables: quest.investmentLinearThreshold (8),
  quest.investmentDiminishingCapExtra (30),
  quest.investmentDiminishingDecay (30).
- balance.ts: new easyFastModeChances(level) tapers Easy's burst/medium
  chance by level band (45/35 -> 30/45 -> 15/55 -> 0/60 at levels
  1-5/6-10/11-15/16+), fixing burst quests rounding down to a trivial
  1 gold/1-2 xp once a hero is a few levels in -- confirmed stretching
  burst's own duration doesn't fix this, since the live per-hour cap
  is the actual bottleneck, not the rounding window.
- generateContractsForHero's guaranteed-burst fallback now respects
  the taper instead of force-injecting a burst offer regardless.
- guild-idler-status.md updated with both writeups plus two backlog
  notes (Mythic tier above Legendary; level-relative scaling explored
  and rejected).
